<BaseLayout title="Editorial policy" description="How Mew & Maple develops, sources, reviews and corrects indoor-cat living guides.">
  <section class="container prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</p>
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p>Mew & Maple produces practical guides about indoor-cat living, enrichment and home setup. Our goal is to explain trade-offs and common risks clearly, not to promise a universal answer for every cat.</p>

    <h2>Sources and factual claims</h2>
    <p>When an article makes a welfare or safety claim, we look for relevant veterinary, academic or established feline-welfare guidance. Sources should support the specific statement, not merely discuss the same broad topic. We distinguish guidance from a manufacturer's product claims and explain important limitations.</p>

    <h2>Animal safety and professional advice</h2>
    <p>Our content is general educational information, not diagnosis or individualized veterinary advice. Changes in appetite, mobility, elimination, behavior or suspected ingestion of foreign material warrant advice from a qualified veterinarian. We do not identify individual cats' medical needs from editorial illustrations.</p>

    <h2>Illustrations and AI assistance</h2>
    <p>Images in the current guide collection are AI-assisted editorial illustrations or diagrams, not photographs of products we purchased, installed or tested. A visual example does not establish that an attachment, houseplant, toy, window mount or piece of furniture is safe. Captions identify known visual limitations where relevant. Drafts may be AI-assisted, but cited claims and safety warnings are separately checked as part of editorial review.</p>

    <h2>Products and commercial relationships</h2>
    <p>We do not claim firsthand product experience, lab testing or veterinarian endorsement without evidence. If future articles include affiliate links, sponsored coverage or products sold by Mew & Maple, the relationship should be disclosed where readers encounter the recommendation. Commercial interests must not be presented as independent test results.</p>

    <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
    <p>Material errors should be corrected promptly when identified. Significant factual changes should be explained or dated on the affected article. Content may also be updated as guidance changes; an update date does not by itself prove a full scientific review was repeated.</p>

    <div class="notice">Pre-launch draft: the legal publisher identity, editorial accountability, public corrections contact and any external expert-review process must be confirmed before release. No veterinary review or formal expert endorsement is claimed.</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
